        "en": "[OSV.dev](https://osv.dev) is a public database of open-source software vulnerabilities that can be\nqueried without authentication. A `POST` request to `https://api.osv.dev/v1/query` with the JSON body\n\n```json\n{\"version\": \"2.2.2\", \"package\": {\"name\": \"flask\", \"ecosystem\": \"PyPI\"}}\n```\n\nreturns `{\"vulns\": [...]}` (each item has an `id` and usually a `summary`), or `{}` if the version\nhas no known vulnerability.\n\nWrite `osv_check.py`, which checks the following dependencies and exits with code `1` if at least\none of them is vulnerable:\n\n```python\nDEPENDENCIES = {\"flask\": \"2.2.2\", \"requests\": \"2.32.3\", \"jinja2\": \"2.11.2\"}\n```\n\nRequirements: a timeout on every call, `raise_for_status()`, a reused session, and clean handling of\nnetwork errors (exit code `2`).\n"
